  "description": "\u00a711.3 \u2014 the alpha channel's own field widths, never measured. alpha DC 5 b, alpha scale 4 b and alpha AC 5 @ 4 b were inherited from v0.6 and were not tunable until now. Arms that change a width also change the byte length, so each is paired with a compensating luma/chroma adjustment that keeps the hash at exactly 32 bytes; the label states the trade. Budget: 54 prefix + alpha_dc + alpha_scale + L\u00b7lb + 2\u00b7C\u00b7cb + A\u00b7ab must land in 249..256 bits.",
